+---
+id: dl-003-applypatch-replace-in-place-move-onto-itself-is-a-no-op-undefined-is-no-value
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch: replace in place, move onto itself is a no-op, undefined is no value"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+# Context
+
+A review of `applyPatch` against RFC 6902 found three deviations, described in task-003.
+
+# Decision
+
+- `replace` assigns at the target (array element or object member) rather than removing and re-adding.
+- `move` whose `from` equals `path` checks that the location exists and changes nothing, root included.
+- A `value` that is `undefined` is treated as missing; sparse patch arrays are validated element by element.
+- Unchanged from dl-002: removing the whole document still throws.
+
+# Consequences
+
+Results match the RFC in these cases and key order is stable under `replace`. Callers who passed
+`value: undefined` now get an error instead of a silently dropped value.
