+
+# Task
+
+Review `applyPatch` against RFC 6902 and fix the deviations found.
+
+## What was done
+
+- `replace` now overwrites the target in place instead of remove then add, so object members keep
+  their position.
+- `move` with identical `from` and `path` (including the whole document) is a no-op once the location
+  is checked to exist; before, moving the root onto itself threw.
+- A `value` of `undefined` on add/replace/test is rejected like a missing `value`; it is not JSON.
+- Holes in a sparse patch array are validated instead of silently skipped.
+- Tests added in `test/patch.test.ts`. Design choices are in decision-log dl-003.
